      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.89,
          "en": "So we need a main entry widget for our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.89,
          "end": 7.41,
          "en": "And for this app I'd like to get started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.41,
          "end": 9.9,
          "en": "with this Categories screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.9,
          "end": 12.51,
          "en": "where we can then select a category",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.51,
          "end": 15.99,
          "en": "and see all the meals that belong to that category.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.99,
          "end": 18.06,
          "en": "And therefore, I'll add a new file here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.06,
          "end": 19.83,
          "en": "in this project lib folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.83,
          "end": 22.05,
          "en": "which I'll name categories.dart,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.05,
          "end": 24.57,
          "en": "because in there I wanna build the widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.57,
          "end": 27.36,
          "en": "that displays all these categories.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.36,
          "end": 29.67,
          "en": "Now inside of categories.dart,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.67,
          "end": 32.73,
          "en": "you should therefore create a new class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.73,
          "end": 36.6,
          "en": "The CategoriesScreen class, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.6,
          "end": 37.92,
          "en": "The name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.92,
          "end": 40.35,
          "en": "And you could also just name it Categories.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.35,
          "end": 43.83,
          "en": "But since this will act as a screen in this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.83,
          "end": 46.47,
          "en": "and we will later have multiple screens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.47,
          "end": 50.73,
          "en": "but also some regular widgets which don't act as screens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.73,
          "end": 53.76,
          "en": "I wanna mark the widgets that will act as screens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.76,
          "end": 56.46,
          "en": "So therefore, this one is the CategoriesScreen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.46,
          "end": 60.42,
          "en": "And we of course extend Stateless or StatefulWidget here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.42,
          "end": 63.09,
          "en": "And here we'll only need a StatelessWidget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.09,
          "end": 66.57,
          "en": "because indeed, there won't be any internal state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.57,
          "end": 70.41,
          "en": "that would need to be managed in that widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.41,
          "end": 74.37,
          "en": "Sure, we'll be able to select a category later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.37,
          "end": 77.43,
          "en": "but as you will see, the navigation to the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.43,
          "end": 79.95,
          "en": "that shows all the meals for the category,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.95,
          "end": 82.47,
          "en": "will not be handled with state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.47,
          "end": 85.28999999999999,
          "en": "but instead with a different mechanism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.28999999999999,
          "end": 87.66,
          "en": "And therefore, this indeed can and should be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.66,
          "end": 88.56,
          "en": "a StatelessWidget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.88,
          "end": 92.37,
          "en": "Now of course, as always, we need the build method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.37,
          "end": 95.293,
          "en": "and we should add a constructor function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.293,
          "end": 99.12,
          "en": "CategoriesScreen is a fitting name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.12,
          "end": 101.1,
          "en": "where we should accept and forward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.1,
          "end": 102.813,
          "en": "the key property as always.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 103.68,
          "end": 105.47999999999999,
          "en": "And here in the build method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 105.47999999999999,
          "end": 108.18,
          "en": "I wanna return the Scaffold widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 108.18,
          "end": 112.59,
          "en": "because I wanna have that default styling that it applies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.59,
          "end": 116.1,
          "en": "I want to be able to add the AppBar at the top and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.1,
          "end": 119.82,
          "en": "And in general, it's very likely in Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 122.01,
          "en": "that if you're building a multi-screen app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.01,
          "end": 125.31,
          "en": "that every screen will use the Scaffold widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.31,
          "end": 127.56,
          "en": "to do its base screen setup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.56,
          "end": 130.89,
          "en": "Because for example, the AppBar often differs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 130.89,
          "end": 133.17,
          "en": "between different screens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.17,
          "end": 135.45,
          "en": "Different screens might have different titles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.45,
          "end": 136.92000000000002,
          "en": "or buttons in the AppBar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 136.92000000000002,
          "end": 139.71,
          "en": "And therefore, being able to set the AppBar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139.71,
          "end": 141.66,
          "en": "or other screen-specific settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.66,
          "end": 143.43,
          "en": "right from inside the screen widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.43,
          "end": 144.93,
          "en": "is a common requirement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 144.93,
          "end": 148.38,
          "en": "And hence, it is quite common to set up the Scaffold widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 148.38,
          "end": 151.203,
          "en": "inside of the screen widget, as we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 152.43,
          "end": 155.46,
          "en": "So here, I will indeed add the AppBar parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 155.46,
          "end": 157.56,
          "en": "and set this to Appbar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 157.56,
          "end": 160.59,
          "en": "So, I'm using the built-in AppBar widget again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 160.59,
          "end": 162.633,
          "en": "as we did it before in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 163.89,
          "end": 165.03,
          "en": "And on that AppBar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 165.03,
          "end": 169.53,
          "en": "I'll set the title parameter to the Text widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 169.53,
          "end": 173.16,
          "en": "and output some text as a title in this AppBar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 173.16,
          "end": 177.36,
          "en": "And the text here could be Pick your category,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 177.36,
          "end": 178.713,
          "en": "or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 180.06,
          "end": 181.56,
          "en": "Now we can also add const here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 181.56,
          "end": 183.72,
          "en": "since this is a constant widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 183.72,
          "end": 185.34,
          "en": "But of course, that's not all I want to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 185.34,
          "end": 187.35,
          "en": "in this Scaffold here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 187.35,
          "end": 190.56,
          "en": "Instead, we also wanna set the body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 190.56,
          "end": 192.27,
          "en": "And the body, as you learned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 192.27,
          "end": 194.79,
          "en": "is the main page content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 194.79,
          "end": 196.38,
          "en": "Now here for the body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 196.38,
          "end": 199.47,
          "en": "I wanna output all these different categories,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 199.47,
          "end": 201.54,
          "en": "which then later can be selected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 201.54,
          "end": 204.3,
          "en": "to move to one of those categories.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 204.3,
          "end": 205.74,
          "en": "And for this app here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 205.74,
          "end": 209.97,
          "en": "I plan to lay out these categories as a grid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 209.97,
          "end": 212.4,
          "en": "And thankfully, creating such a grid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 212.4,
          "end": 215.07,
          "en": "is also quite straightforward in Flutter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 215.07,
          "end": 217.56,
          "en": "because it does not just offer a ListView",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 217.56,
          "end": 220.45499999999998,
          "en": "for rendering a list, but also a GridView for,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 220.45499999999998,
          "end": 224.34,
          "en": "you guessed it, rendering a grid of items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 224.34,
          "end": 226.86,
          "en": "And here, just as with the ListView,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 226.86,
          "end": 229.8,
          "en": "you also have a builder constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 229.8,
          "end": 232.86,
          "en": "which would allow you to build the grid dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 232.86,
          "end": 237.86,
          "en": "if you had a potentially very long list of grid items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 238.23,
          "end": 239.25,
          "en": "But alternatively,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 239.25,
          "end": 242.58,
          "en": "you can also instantiate the grid view widget like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 242.58,
          "end": 246.15,
          "en": "to not get this possible performance optimization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 246.15,
          "end": 248.79,
          "en": "of only rendering what's visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 248.79,
          "end": 251.7,
          "en": "But here, I won't have that many categories,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 251.7,
          "end": 254.04,
          "en": "so that performance optimization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 254.04,
          "end": 256.41,
          "en": "wouldn't really kick in anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 256.41,
          "end": 258.3,
          "en": "And therefore I'll use this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 258.3,
          "end": 260.91,
          "en": "where I can directly set my children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 260.91,
          "end": 264.27,
          "en": "So, the items that should be displayed in the grid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 264.27,
          "end": 267.63,
          "en": "Now, GridView also needs something else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 267.63,
          "end": 269.28,
          "en": "As you can see in this error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 269.28,
          "end": 273.39,
          "en": "It needs a gridDelegate, which should be set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 273.39,
          "end": 275.73,
          "en": "And therefore, besides setting the children,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 275.73,
          "end": 277.8,
          "en": "which we will soon do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 277.8,
          "end": 282.48,
          "en": "you also must add the gridDelegate parameter here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 282.48,
          "end": 286.29,
          "en": "And this is a parameter which might sound quite strange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 286.29,
          "end": 288.03,
          "en": "but in the end, if you hover over it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 288.03,
          "end": 291.18,
          "en": "you learn that this in the end simply controls the layout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 291.18,
          "end": 293.19,
          "en": "of the GridView items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 293.19,
          "end": 295.05,
          "en": "And here, I'll create a grid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 295.05,
          "end": 300.05,
          "en": "with this SliverGridDelegateWithFixedCrossAxisCount option,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 300.6,
          "end": 303.12,
          "en": "which is a very complex way of saying that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 303.12,
          "end": 305.82,
          "en": "I can, in the end, set the number of columns",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 305.82,
          "end": 307.233,
          "en": "which I want to have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 308.22,
          "end": 311.88,
          "en": "So here, I can set my CrossAxisCount to 2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 311.88,
          "end": 314.73,
          "en": "And since by default, the GridView mainAxis",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 314.73,
          "end": 319.08,
          "en": "is from top to bottom, the crossAxis is from left to right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 319.08,
          "end": 323.04,
          "en": "So if I set this to 2, I get two columns next to each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 323.04,
          "end": 326.28,
          "en": "So, horizontally, I have these two columns.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 326.28,
          "end": 330.33,
          "en": "Now with that set here, we can also set a childAspectRatio,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 330.33,
          "end": 333.51,
          "en": "which will impact the sizing of those GridView items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 333.51,
          "end": 336.65999999999997,
          "en": "And here, I'll set this two 3 divided by 2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 336.65999999999997,
          "end": 340.323,
          "en": "Two in the end, dynamically derive a three to two ratio.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 341.15999999999997,
          "end": 344.31,
          "en": "Alternatively, you could also manually set this to 1.5.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 344.31,
          "end": 346.77,
          "en": "I'm just using this notation to make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 346.77,
          "end": 348.81,
          "en": "that this in the end is the aspect ratio",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 348.81,
          "end": 350.22,
          "en": "which I want to have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 350.22,
          "end": 353.76,
          "en": "And I'll also set a crossAxisSpacing of 20,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 353.76,
          "end": 356.073,
          "en": "to have some spacing between the columns,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 357.03,
          "end": 359.82,
          "en": "and a mainAxisSpacing of 20 as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 359.82,
          "end": 363.66,
          "en": "so that I have a spacing of 20 pixels horizontally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 363.66,
          "end": 366.963,
          "en": "between my items, and vertically between my grid items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 368.4,
          "end": 371.613,
          "en": "And this can then also be turned into a const object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 372.84,
          "end": 374.88,
          "en": "So, that's the grid configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 374.88,
          "end": 377.67,
          "en": "Now we can add our grid items here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 377.67,
          "end": 380.16,
          "en": "And I'll add the actual data soon enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 380.16,
